mechanism.summary:
A tiny WEBrick servlet reflects ?x=<value> into the response header X-Reflected. WEBrick::HTTPResponse#send_header runs check_header(value) on each header value at write time. CVE-2017-17742 (ruby 2.5.1) added check_header raising InvalidHeader when `header_value =~ /
/` -- matching only the full CR-LF PAIR, so an isolated CR () or isolated LF (
) slips through and still splits the header stream (CVE-2019-16254 residual). Ruby 2.5.8 changed the check to `/[
]/ =~ header_value`, rejecting ANY isolated CR or LF. On InvalidHeader, send_header clears @header/@cookies, sets a 500 error, and retries -> a blocked payload emits an error page WITHOUT the injected flag.

