original = full CR-LF pair (
); residual = isolated LF (
). Same /[
]/ char class; the incompleteness is the MISSED CHARACTER FORM (isolated CR/LF vs the CRLF pair), NOT a different sink

provenance.notes:
Version boundary confirmed by grepping the bundled webrick httpresponse.rb inside each ruby:2.5.x image: V0 (2.5.0) no check_header; V1 (2.5.1) check_header =~ /
/ (CRLF pair only, lone /
 pass); V2 (2.5.8) check_header /[
]/ (any CR/LF). The webrick standalone gem tags skip the incomplete state (1.4.2=no check -> 1.4.4=complete /[
]/), so ruby:2.5.x base images are used. Same regular-header sink both CVEs; residual = isolated LF that V1's pair-only regex misses.
